  "notes": "Cash-basis village; Water and Sewer are business-type (Proprietary column of p1-p2, p5-p8). Governmental data from p4 Total column (General + Street); business-type from p6 (Water, Sewer, Total column). Governmental interest income 10,535 and business-type interest income 4,539, loan payments 61,543, interest expense 28,124 and capital outlay 30,000 are printed below the statements' total lines (outside_printed_total). Governmental transfers (673) out; proprietary transfers net +673. Personnel/operating/supplies are object lines with no function: General Fund column as general government and Street Fund column (operating 12,450, supplies 20,222) as streets/highways, split by column (split_from), with review. Balance sheet uses p1 Total column (governmental + proprietary); liabilities none. Detail: only the all-funds budgetary schedule (p9) exists; no per-fund columns, so lines are recorded as fund 'All funds' with fund_type per line; Water and Sewer are business-type lines with budgets (department = Water/Sewer). Taxes, Charges for services, Interest and Other lines are split by fund type/tax type using breakdowns printed on p2/p4/p6 (budget amount left null on split lines; whole-line final budgets: Taxes 58,065, Charges 136,000, Interest 2,000, Other 0). Transfers are other-financing lines (+673 in, -673 out), which the printed totals include. Water/Sewer budget lines include debt service and capital but are not itemized. Pages 7-8 (proprietary cash flow statement) agree with p6 and are not recorded separately. Read pages 1-9 of 9 Audit3 fix: p9 Transfers receipts 673 recorded as business-type (the proprietary funds receive the net 673 per p6; governmental funds transfer it out per p4)."
